James was trying to serve a PDF file, "PROSPER_Technical_Documentation.pdf," from the `www` directory in his Shiny app, but encountered "Not Found" errors with both attempted URLs. I clarified that the correct URL to access the PDF should not include `/www/` and should instead be `http://127.0.0.1:6568/PROSPER_Technical_Documentation.pdf`. I also explained that when launching the app directly with `shinyApp(ui, server)`, the `www` directory might not be automatically recognized. I recommended explicitly registering the directory using `addResourcePath()` and provided a code example to access the PDF through a link in the app, which should then work at the corrected URL.
